      "message": "ucer, **no import of `semkg_contract`**.\n\n**What it does (what I read and copied):**\n\n- The contract I read declares `CONTRACT_VERSION = 1` with\n  `can_transition(old, new) = (old, new) in {('new','paid'), ('new','cancelled')}`.\n- `producer.py` records `CONTRACT_VERSION = 1` and a module-level `frozenset` `_ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS = {(\"new\",\"paid\"), (\"new\",\"cancelled\")}`, and reimplements `can_transition(old, new)` as a pure membership test over that set \u2014 semantically identical to the contract, with the assumption (version 1 transition table) preserved inline in the docstrings.\n- Therefore `can_transition('paid', 'refunded')` returns **`False`** under v1. No v2 behavior was implemented because the contract file I read is version 1; if a v2 contract is ever present it must be read and its transitions copied in explicitly.\n\nI attempted a small local parity check but the sandbox rejected every `run_command` invocation, so no tests were executed. Changes are confined to the attempt directory."
